## Critical Invariants

1. Preflight with `project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)`;
   bare `project_config()` stays the role-optional config surface.
   Every child has explicit role, background mode, model, and in-policy
   Codex/Qwen reasoning effort.
2. Workers use compact, task-specific projections. Skip routine
   `summary()`, `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`; scoped schema only
   repairs an unknown call.
3. Default to `task-board spawn observe RUN --until terminal --format compact`,
   then route its handoff. Other reads are for barriers, replay/follow,
   diagnosis.
4. The Orchestrator owns producer -> reviewer -> rework -> reviewer until the
   configured review policy is satisfied and the board reaches `done`.
   `to-review` is a routing trigger, not human acceptance.
5. Handoff needs a task-scoped outcome and `task-board handoff TASK-ID
   --role ROLE`. Early exits and intermediate parked states are
   retried, or rerouted through a focused child;
   routine work is never handed to the human.
6. `blocked` needs an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved
